<!--
    FS25_SellPrices price table

    On first start this file is copied to  <user>/Documents/My Games/FarmingSimulator2025/modSettings/FS25_SellPrices/prices.xml
    Edit that copy; the one inside the mod zip is only the default. After editing, restart the savegame,
    or type  spReload  in the developer console to apply it live (server / single player).

    price   = sell price in EUR per 1000 L (per 1000 pieces for piece goods) on HARD economic difficulty,
              i.e. fillType pricePerLiter x 1000, before seasonal factor and selling-point priceScale.
    scale   = alternative to price: multiply the price the game/map defines (e.g. scale="0.5").
    factors = optional, 12 seasonal factors in period order 1..12 (early spring .. late winter),
              replaces the curve of the base game / map. Without it the original curve is kept.

    Selling points keep their own priceScale (e.g. HB bales x0.8, root crops x1.2 at the animal dealer).
    <station> overrides it for one selling point and fillType; xmlFilename is matched as a path suffix,
    run spDump to see the xmlFilename of every selling point.

    Snapshot: base game 1.23.1 + Hof Bergmann 1.5.0.0 Beta2 (2026-09-29). Values below equal the current
    game prices, so this table changes nothing until you edit it.  "/t" comments = EUR per tonne.
-->
